WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.269
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B two.

2
00:00:05.569 --> 00:00:08.955
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.255 --> 00:00:15.983
Unit three: Passive Voice (advanced). Today you will use passive forms with continuous, perfect and modal verbs.

4
00:00:16.283 --> 00:00:18.935
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:22.970
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.817 --> 00:00:25.004
Is being built.

7
00:00:26.017 --> 00:00:29.050
Is being built means present continuous passive.

8
00:00:29.650 --> 00:00:31.174
A bridge is being built.

9
00:00:31.783 --> 00:00:34.703
Your turn. Say: Is being built.

10
00:00:37.567 --> 00:00:38.695
Is being built.

11
00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:40.556
Has been made.

12
00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:43.991
Has been made means present perfect passive.

13
00:00:44.583 --> 00:00:46.130
It has been made by hand.

14
00:00:46.717 --> 00:00:49.183
Your turn. Say: Has been made.

15
00:00:52.033 --> 00:00:53.313
Has been made.

16
00:00:54.050 --> 00:00:55.388
Will be completed.

17
00:00:56.383 --> 00:00:58.499
Will be completed means future passive.

18
00:00:59.083 --> 00:01:00.909
It will be completed in May.

19
00:01:01.517 --> 00:01:04.181
Your turn. Say: Will be completed.

20
00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:08.452
Will be completed.

21
00:01:09.217 --> 00:01:10.450
Modal passive.

22
00:01:11.450 --> 00:01:15.040
Modal passive means modal + be + past participle.

23
00:01:15.650 --> 00:01:16.941
It must be done.

24
00:01:17.550 --> 00:01:20.353
Your turn. Say: Modal passive.

25
00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:24.491
Modal passive.

26
00:01:25.250 --> 00:01:26.750
Continuous passive.

27
00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:31.642
Continuous passive means be + being + past participle.

28
00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:33.588
It is being repaired.

29
00:01:34.183 --> 00:01:37.416
Your turn. Say: Continuous passive.

30
00:01:40.267 --> 00:01:41.767
Continuous passive.

31
00:01:42.517 --> 00:01:43.878
Perfect passive.

32
00:01:44.883 --> 00:01:48.485
Perfect passive means have + been + past participle.

33
00:01:49.083 --> 00:01:50.444
It has been repaired.

34
00:01:51.050 --> 00:01:53.911
Your turn. Say: Perfect passive.

35
00:01:56.767 --> 00:01:58.035
Perfect passive.

36
00:01:58.783 --> 00:01:59.645
Agent.

37
00:02:00.650 --> 00:02:02.824
Agent means the doer of an action.

38
00:02:03.417 --> 00:02:05.021
The agent follows by.

39
00:02:05.617 --> 00:02:08.095
Your turn. Say: Agent.

40
00:02:10.933 --> 00:02:11.783
Agent.

41
00:02:12.550 --> 00:02:13.621
Process.

42
00:02:14.617 --> 00:02:16.709
Process means a series of steps.

43
00:02:17.317 --> 00:02:18.980
The process is described.

44
00:02:19.583 --> 00:02:21.957
Your turn. Say: Process.

45
00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:25.778
Process.

46
00:02:26.567 --> 00:02:30.786
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:34.741
Visal, describe something that is being built in your city.

48
00:02:35.850 --> 00:02:49.058
A new bridge is being built over the river. This is the present continuous passive: is or are being plus the past participle. It focuses on the process, not the builders.

49
00:02:50.150 --> 00:02:51.894
What about other tenses?

50
00:02:52.983 --> 00:03:05.823
Present perfect: The road has been repaired. Future: The work will be completed in May. Modal: It must be finished soon. Past perfect: The plan had been approved.

51
00:03:06.917 --> 00:03:08.591
When do we mention the agent?

52
00:03:09.683 --> 00:03:23.333
Only when it is important, using by: The painting was restored by experts. Otherwise we omit it. The passive suits reports, news and science, where the action matters more than the actor.

53
00:03:24.467 --> 00:03:25.828
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:26.683 --> 00:03:31.643
Grammar focus: Advanced passive: be plus past participle in all tenses.

55
00:03:31.943 --> 00:03:33.130
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:33.817 --> 00:03:36.199
A new bridge is being built over the river.

57
00:03:37.083 --> 00:03:39.141
The road has been repaired by the council.

58
00:03:40.050 --> 00:03:42.061
The work will be completed in May.

59
00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:53.338
Passive = be + past participle, with the tense on be: is being built, has been made, will be completed, must be done. Add by + agent only if it matters.

60
00:03:54.083 --> 00:03:57.757
Be careful! Don't say: The road is repairing now.

61
00:03:59.700 --> 00:04:02.408
Say: The road is being repaired now.

62
00:04:02.708 --> 00:04:04.603
Use the continuous passive.

63
00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:08.145
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:08.933 --> 00:04:10.422
Process, Not People.

65
00:04:10.722 --> 00:04:13.534
A new bridge is being built over the river in my city.

66
00:04:14.533 --> 00:04:17.392
The old road has been repaired by the local council.

67
00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:20.214
The work will be completed in May.

68
00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:24.128
The plan had been approved before the budget was announced.

69
00:04:25.133 --> 00:04:28.294
The passive focuses on the process rather than on the people.

70
00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:33.657
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:34.517 --> 00:04:36.261
The road blank at the moment.

72
00:04:36.561 --> 00:04:40.853
A, is repairing. B, is being repaired. C, has repaired.

73
00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:46.957
The answer is B: is being repaired.

74
00:04:48.117 --> 00:04:49.872
The report blank by Friday.

75
00:04:50.172 --> 00:04:54.174
A, will be finished. B, will finished. C, is finishing.

76
00:04:57.733 --> 00:05:00.116
The answer is A: will be finished.

77
00:05:01.250 --> 00:05:02.971
The bridge blank last year.

78
00:05:03.271 --> 00:05:06.704
A, was built. B, built. C, was build.

79
00:05:10.267 --> 00:05:12.324
The answer is A: was built.

80
00:05:13.483 --> 00:05:15.169
Which is a modal passive?

81
00:05:15.469 --> 00:05:19.216
A, It must be done.. B, It is done.. C, It did..

82
00:05:22.767 --> 00:05:25.300
The answer is A: It must be done..

83
00:05:26.450 --> 00:05:29.471
According to the reading, when will the work finish?

84
00:05:29.771 --> 00:05:33.076
A, in May. B, in June. C, tomorrow.

85
00:05:36.633 --> 00:05:39.004
The answer is A: in May.

86
00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:43.549
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:44.383 --> 00:05:47.242
Write a sentence using 'has been' in the passive voice.

88
00:05:56.050 --> 00:05:57.817
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:58.117 --> 00:06:10.664
The new road in my town has been repaired. It has been closed for months, and it will be reopened next week. I use has been plus the past participle because the result matters more than the workers.

90
00:06:10.964 --> 00:06:12.650
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:13.550 --> 00:06:20.707
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and advanced passive: be plus past participle in all tenses.

92
00:06:21.007 --> 00:06:25.668
Today's value is public engagement. Share knowledge so that everyone can learn from it.

93
00:06:25.968 --> 00:06:28.376
See you in Unit four. Goodbye!

94
00:06:28.676 --> 00:06:32.153
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

